      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_e8245298f486d168f88be7c7ab856b4dfe2a3183fc23e03aaec8bed76d54e406",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A trace-formula analogy survives only after its local invariants are checked: graph-diagonal transversality produces return-map determinant weights, while the Riemann secondary-zeta setting has double poles where the compared Selberg machinery has simple ones, forcing separate analytic treatment.",
