    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_f4842fb4826cbd416d92802c8efb7d7112a8f01f7568fc0aa6b843a6b464e936",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Large-value control is regime-sensitive: zero-density reductions use frequencies of large or simultaneous Dirichlet-polynomial values, critical-line moments or pointwise inputs can constrain those tails, and prime-sum majorants provide a separate conditional route from zeta size to tractable high-moment tail bounds. No single estimator dominates every parameter range.",
